<hr>
<h2>Content Tabs</h2>
<h3>General Content Tabs (<code>:::tabs</code>)</h3>
<p><code>:::tabs</code> presents alternative content blocks. Each <code>::tab</code> takes a required <code>label</code> and an optional <code>icon</code> (Lucide or Bootstrap Icons, same rules as callouts), and is closed with <code>::</code>. Here, a comparison of rendering strategies:</p>
<div class="mdrs-tabs">
  <div class="mdrs-tabs-header" role="tablist">
    <div class="mdrs-tabs-nav">
      <button type="button" role="tab" class="mdrs-tab mdrs-is-active" data-mdrs-tab-label="Server-Side Rendering (SSR)" aria-selected="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="mdrs-icon mdrs-icon-server" aria-hidden="true"><rect width="20" height="8" x="2" y="2" rx="2" ry="2"/><rect width="20" height="8" x="2" y="14" rx="2" ry="2"/><line x1="6" x2="6.01" y1="6" y2="6"/><line x1="6" x2="6.01" y1="18" y2="18"/></svg>Server-Side Rendering (SSR)</button><button type="button" role="tab" class="mdrs-tab" data-mdrs-tab-label="Client-Side Rendering (CSR)" aria-selected="false"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="mdrs-icon mdrs-icon-monitor" aria-hidden="true"><rect width="20" height="14" x="2" y="3" rx="2"/><line x1="8" x2="16" y1="21" y2="21"/><line x1="12" x2="12" y1="17" y2="21"/></svg>Client-Side Rendering (CSR)</button>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="mdrs-tabs-body">
    <div role="tabpanel" class="mdrs-tab-panel"><p>SSR generates the full HTML on the server before sending it to the browser. The page is immediately readable: search engines index real content, and users on slow connections see meaningful output without waiting for JavaScript to boot.</p>
<h4>When to use SSR</h4>
<div class="mdrs-steps">
<ol class="mdrs-steps-list">
<li class="mdrs-step">Content-heavy pages where SEO matters (blogs, documentation, landing pages).</li>
<li class="mdrs-step">Users on low-powered devices or constrained networks.</li>
<li class="mdrs-step">Pages where time-to-first-byte is more important than interactivity latency.</li>
</ol>
</div></div><div role="tabpanel" class="mdrs-tab-panel" hidden><p>CSR ships a minimal HTML shell and builds the page entirely in the browser via JavaScript. The initial load is faster in bytes, but the page is blank until the framework hydrates, making it unsuitable for content that needs to be indexed or immediately visible.</p>
<h4>When to use CSR</h4>
<div class="mdrs-steps">
<ol class="mdrs-steps-list">
<li class="mdrs-step">Highly interactive dashboards or real-time applications.</li>
<li class="mdrs-step">Authenticated pages behind a login wall (no SEO needed).</li>
<li class="mdrs-step">Single-page apps where subsequent navigation speed matters more than first paint.</li>
</ol>
</div></div>
  </div>
</div><h3>Code Snippets (<code>:::snippets</code>)</h3>
<p><code>:::snippets</code> is the code-oriented variant: it adds copy and download controls for the active tab. The optional <code>key</code> synchronizes every snippet group that shares it. Pick your package manager once, and every code block updates:</p>
<div class="mdrs-snippets" data-mdrs-tab-key="bundler">
  <div class="mdrs-snippets-header hljs" role="tablist">
    <div class="mdrs-snippets-nav">
      <button type="button" role="tab" class="mdrs-tab mdrs-is-active" data-mdrs-tab-label="bun" aria-selected="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="mdrs-icon mdrs-icon-terminal" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 19h8"/><path d="m4 17 6-6-6-6"/></svg>bun</button><button type="button" role="tab" class="mdrs-tab" data-mdrs-tab-label="npm" aria-selected="false"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="mdrs-icon mdrs-icon-package" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M11 21.73a2 2 0 0 0 2 0l7-4A2 2 0 0 0 21 16V8a2 2 0 0 0-1-1.73l-7-4a2 2 0 0 0-2 0l-7 4A2 2 0 0 0 3 8v8a2 2 0 0 0 1 1.73z"/><path d="M12 22V12"/><polyline points="3.29 7 12 12 20.71 7"/><path d="m7.5 4.27 9 5.15"/></svg>npm</button><button type="button" role="tab" class="mdrs-tab" data-mdrs-tab-label="pnpm" aria-selected="false"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="mdrs-icon mdrs-icon-package" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M11 21.73a2 2 0 0 0 2 0l7-4A2 2 0 0 0 21 16V8a2 2 0 0 0-1-1.73l-7-4a2 2 0 0 0-2 0l-7 4A2 2 0 0 0 3 8v8a2 2 0 0 0 1 1.73z"/><path d="M12 22V12"/><polyline points="3.29 7 12 12 20.71 7"/><path d="m7.5 4.27 9 5.15"/></svg>pnpm</button><button type="button" role="tab" class="mdrs-tab" data-mdrs-tab-label="yarn" aria-selected="false"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="mdrs-icon mdrs-icon-package" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M11 21.73a2 2 0 0 0 2 0l7-4A2 2 0 0 0 21 16V8a2 2 0 0 0-1-1.73l-7-4a2 2 0 0 0-2 0l-7 4A2 2 0 0 0 3 8v8a2 2 0 0 0 1 1.73z"/><path d="M12 22V12"/><polyline points="3.29 7 12 12 20.71 7"/><path d="m7.5 4.27 9 5.15"/></svg>yarn</button>
    </div>
